Skiff — licensing
=================

Skiff is not under a single license. Which one applies depends on which part of
the repository you are looking at.

  packages/core/          Apache License 2.0
  everything else         GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only

Why the split
-------------

`packages/core` is the engine: SSH session management, the encrypted vault,
session recording, the tamper-evident audit log, and the database layer. It is
a library, and it is deliberately permissive so it can be shared across every
build of Skiff — including builds that are not themselves open source.

Everything built on top of that engine — the desktop app, the web UI, the API
server — stays under the AGPL. That is what stops someone taking Skiff, running
it as a closed commercial service, and giving nothing back. The protection is
on the product, not on the library.

What this means for you
-----------------------

Using Skiff:        nothing changes. The application is AGPL, as it always was.
Contributing:       your contribution is licensed under whichever license
                    applies to the files you touch.
Building on core:   Apache 2.0. No obligation to publish your source, and an
                    explicit patent grant.

